Literary theory and criticism (@literary-theory-and-criticism: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_4S7B496C6HPN4AK709BK28CDV1
Literary theory examines how texts, authors, readers, forms, and contexts participate in the production of meaning and value. This material compares approaches to genre, narrative, language, interpretation, authorship, reception, and criticism through their application to works. Build from close reading toward the concepts needed by a chosen question, making assumptions and disagreements explicit. Share aesthetic and hermeneutic questions with Philosophy and historical or social explanations with History and Sociology.

**Parent:** [Literature](../Literature.lingua#r_68XTEFTFVR5ZPB68D6E1XK0SR3).
